{
  "meta": {
    "title": "ColdFire V4e (MCF5441x) instruction encodings: ISA_A/B/C, EMAC, FPU",
    "sources": {
      "CFPRM": "ColdFire Family Programmer's Reference Manual, Rev. 2, 07/2001 (out/refs/CFPRM). Page numbers are PDF pages (out/refs/CFPRM/pages/pNNNN.txt).",
      "RM": "MCF5441x Reference Manual (out/refs/MCF5441XRM). Page numbers are PDF pages."
    },
    "notes": [
      "The table holds encodings only: no firmware bytes.",
      "enc: one 16-character pattern per fixed instruction word (opword, then fixed extension words); spaces are ignored. '0'/'1' are fixed bits, '-' is don't-care, a letter names a field bit (a letter used several times in one word forms one field, msb first).",
      "fields: composite fields, a string of letters concatenated msb first; a '~' before a letter inverts that bit.",
      "size: a fixed size letter, '' for unsized, or {f, map, else} mapping a field value to a size (a value missing from the map, with no else, is an illegal encoding).",
      "allow: {field: [values]} restricts a field; eq/ne compare two fields.",
      "deny: illegal combinations: ops maps an operand index to EA modes, sizes and fields optionally narrow the rule.",
      "An instruction is at most 3 words (48 bits), CFPRM p.35 (2.1): the generator enforces this for every EA combination.",
      "MCF5441x has no FPU: the D0 hardware configuration loaded at reset has FPU=0, RM p.106-107 (3.3.4.15), and RM p.46 (1.7.1) lists no FPU. The FPU forms are decoded for completeness; on this device they take the line-F exception.",
      "ISA_C additions BITREV, BYTEREV, FF1 are named in RM p.97 (Table 3-4) and timed in RM p.113; CFPRM Rev. 2 predates ISA_C and has no encoding page for them. Their encodings (0x00C0/0x02C0/0x04C0 | Dx) are confirmed against the firmware images by the oracle (tools/cfisa/oracle.py).",
      "STLDSR (ISA_A+/ISA_C) is not described by either local manual and is not included.",
      "FNOP (0xF280 0x0000) is FBF.W with displacement 0 (CFPRM p.229); it decodes as fbf.w."
    ]
  },
